  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Sustaining the Expansion of the Overseas Health Assessment and Management of U.S.-Bound Refugees, Non-Immigrant Visa Applicants and other Migrant Populations</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">IOM&#x2019;s global response to COVID-19 aims to limit human-to-human transmission, minimize the impact of COVID-19 in vulnerable countries with limited preparedness capacity, and reduce specific threats that pose current and future risk to the United States. IOM will also implement a number of public health interventions for Ukrainian and Afghan migrants and refugees, faced with mounting health needs of these populations.</narrative>
  </description>
